{"agent_id":"pp3g-MS88-review-synthesize-the-one-shot-architectural-reviews","agent_seq":7,"timestamp":"2026-08-15T01:00:59.990696158Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"717d91fe-b320-4642-ae86-1b6f34ea1837","comment_uuid":"f4586ba9-562e-4a7e-a99f-a92b689b6be2","author":"pp3g-MS88-review-synthesize-the-one-shot-architectural-reviews","content":"Result: Synthesis delivered at docs/research/Tools Distribution Architecture Synthesis.md (865 lines, commit 8cd6674 with [#373]).\n\nWHAT WAS DONE: Read the reviews file IN FULL (2,874 lines) plus the input brief (256 lines). Produced a grounded synthesis covering all six required parts.\n\n1. REVIEWERS (7 labeled; note: issue text said '8+ + large unlabeled' but the file has 7 labeled reviews — Qwen3.8-Max IS the large one at L1559-2873; no unlabeled section exists): ChatGPT (L4-730, Option F = D+B-lite+A), Deepseek V4 Pro 0813 (L733-1012, D+E hybrid with .tools-pin + manifest), Claude Sonnet 5 High (L1015-1035, D + C for wrappers only), Gemini 3.6 Flash (L1038-1177, D + lightweight pinning), GLM-5.2 (L1180-1427, phased D, sync-tooling.sh as Class-2 mechanism), Kimi Instant (L1431-1556, Option D+ = D+C-symlinks+B-discipline), Qwen3.8-Max (L1559-2873, D frame + C where tested + B-lite + E bridge).\n2. CONVERGENCE (7/7): refined diagnosis (multiple writable copies, no enforced single source/flow/pinning — NOT the layer split); single-copy precedent as empirical anchor; D as target architecture; E interim-only; A rejected as general (ownership/cadence coupling); full B rejected but B-lite invariants adopted; bug fixes independent of architecture; reverse-sync first.\n3. DIVERGENCE: Class-1 mechanism (symlinks-now [Kimi, Claude-wrappers] vs user-level single-copy [Deepseek/Gemini/ChatGPT/GLM] vs test-first fast-follow); flow direction (Tools->live vs GLM's live->Tools Option F); hybrid-vs-pure-D (GLM argues D is already a per-class hybrid); state-machine disposition (Deepseek/Qwen drop, GLM narrowed-for-Class-2, ChatGPT don't invest); Tools placement (Qwen uniquely challenges repo-of-repos); whitelist policy (Qwen only).\n4. STRENGTH/RISK per position with cross-reviewer support — D strongest (evidence-based, graceful degradation), D+/C link-first strongest drift elimination but untested-loader risk, A disqualifying ownership coupling + GLM's item-7 falsification, B full over-engineered, C elegant but load-bearing untested assumptions.\n5. RECOMMENDED SYNTHESIS: phased D with staged C promotion — Phase 0 fix bugs now (schema-level precedence fix per Qwen), Phase 1 reverse-sync, Phase 2 blocking verification tests (user-level guard loading, symlink plugin loading, init --force collateral, init-deploys-guards), Phase 3 three classes (wrappers symlinked now, guard/model plugins user-level-then-symlink-after-test, Class 2 pinned copy-out with committed sha256 manifest and NO permanent state machine, Class 3 never synced), Phase 4 retire transitional machinery, Phase 5 optional enforcement. 7 open operator decision points listed (flow direction, Class-1 mechanism, guard locus, state-machine disposition, Tools placement, whitelist policy, machinery scale).\n6. WHAT-NOT-TESTED: 16 items compiled from every reviewer's verification-gap list; the four blocking tests for the D migration are called out.\n\nEvery claim cites reviewer + line/section; the only file written is the synthesis. Verified: no stubs, commit includes only the synthesis file.","created_at":"2026-08-15T01:00:59.982804976Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:zfRf1NH9eo5AoX0lfNPNNf6CqBLPpcGxZIpd5G6DvU4","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgbTM+iAj4zJCdlVPrxZ0C7M6XMWVP2m5mknfgF8Urdr8AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA34wtBgVTWy6wnZ1S/lGGa2mqUFT+aZPhE6XrsBEab+6Qvu2+uSPpCh4Du2lP4sNYqFvUtWSrKhvWrVe4gILgAg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:zfRf1NH9eo5AoX0lfNPNNf6CqBLPpcGxZIpd5G6DvU4","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgbTM+iAj4zJCdlVPrxZ0C7M6XMWVP2m5mkn